<p>Russia’s Foreign Ministry said it warned diplomatic missions and representatives of international organizations to prepare to evacuate staff from Kyiv if Moscow launches a mass or “retaliatory” strike in response to any Ukrainian attempt to disrupt Russia’s May 9 Victory Day commemorations in Moscow. The warning came as Russia’s announced May 8-9 Victory Day ceasefire and Ukrainian calls for a broader halt remained disputed, with reports saying attacks continued on both sides.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/pkZQLcmH4XkZafyvsDoGKKznSY5I6wLb6sfQkRWukAlajLU4ReVspaPxBeNYcO8iTQnq2uQ4UxWGFX7v_hB4wcltCU-5kLZURhrI3dEGf748GBdxx1avxP_RjvaDOIX-6oVQ-YmcIQ7Zl4ELSPdUc3qGzbus_JrvyebqIQe95KvMbOU4r_tJS7iPlGCRe1x-v4eRvT_HBc4mUXAwWbgRsXPvCnARwxDhMK1VrlLMZAg4ggC5Aixlvps' alt='A full moon rises over Kyiv during an air raid alarm on May 2, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Security measures: Reports said Moscow tightened security before the parade amid drone fears, and Russian authorities said they downed about 50 Ukrainian drones overnight.</li><li>Ukraine’s counteroffer: Zelensky offered a truce before, during and potentially after the anniversary, contingent on Russia ceasing fire.</li><li>Target wording: Russian state-linked accounts quoted the warning as referring to Kyiv “decision-making centers,” while SCMP said Moscow did not publicly elaborate on the threat.</li></ul><blockquote>The Russian Ministry of Foreign Affairs strongly urges the authorities of your country...to treat this statement with the utmost responsibility and ensure the timely evacuation from the city of Kyiv of the personnel of diplomatic and other representations in connection with the inevitability of a retaliatory strike on Kyiv by Russia&#x27;s Armed Forces - Maria Zakharova</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Russian Foreign Ministry: Zakharova linked the warning to what Moscow called Zelensky’s aggressive statements and criticized EU countries present at the Armenia meeting for not